            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: what did pakṣi mean?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: పెరుగు",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "పెరుగు (perugu) — \"curd\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "పెరుగు (perugu) is set curd: పాలు left overnight with a spoonful of yesterday's పెరుగు (perugu) stirred in. It closes almost every meal in a Telugu house, and a bhōjanaṁ without it is thought unfinished."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The word is inherited, and Telugu uses the same shape for what curd does and for what anything does when it grows. Curd is milk that grew."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A గేదె's పాలు set thicker than a cow's, which is one reason a village that keeps buffaloes is in no hurry to change."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The first thing in the kitchen."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
