        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: నూనె",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "నూనె (nūne) — \"oil\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "నూనె (nūne) is oil pressed from seeds — groundnut, sesame, sunflower — and it is what a kitchen cooks with on the days it is not cooking with నెయ్యి (neyyi)."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The word is inherited, and Telugu keeps it firmly apart from నెయ్యి (neyyi). One comes from an animal and one comes from a విత్తనం, and no cook mixes the two up."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "నూనె (nūne) also works outside the kitchen. It is what goes into a దీపం, and a house that has run out of it sits in the dark."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Three."
            }
          ]
        },
