            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: what did cakkera mean?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: మిరప",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "మిరప (mirapa) — \"a chilli\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "మిరప (mirapa) is the chilli, and it is the newest thing in this kitchen by several thousand years. The plant crossed from the Americas on Portuguese ships and reached the coast about four hundred years ago."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The word is older than the plant it names. It belonged to black pepper first, and when the new pod arrived and took over the job of making food hot, the name went with the job rather than staying with the plant."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Andhra cooking is built on it now, and a kitchen there measures itself by how much మిరప (mirapa) it can carry. Five things, and the person at the stove will ask your పేరు before the meal is over."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Five: పెరుగు (perugu), నెయ్యి (neyyi), నూనె (nūne), చక్కెర (cakkera), మిరప (mirapa). Enough to name what a kitchen holds while somebody asks you your పేరు."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
